-- title:
--   From HTo GStage Mass Split Succ
-- statement:
--   **A nonterminal stage splits according to the next Boolean tail bit.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `psi_bi` be a quantum state, let `family` be an indexed polynomial family, and let natural numbers `k` and `ell` satisfy $\ell<k$. The remaining type at stage `ell` has length $k-\ell$, and its first bit can be separated from the remaining tail. The exact recurrence identity is
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{fromHToGStageMass}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},k,\ell)
--   =
--   \sum_{(b,\tau)\in\{0,1\}\times\{0,1\}^{k-(\ell+1)}}
--   \operatorname{fromHToGTailStageMass}\!\left(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},\ell,\operatorname{prependTypeBit}(b,\tau)\right).
--   $$
--
--   Thus the full stage mass is the sum of the tail-stage masses indexed by the next Boolean bit and the shorter type pattern. This is the combinatorial split used by `fromHToGStageMass_eq_adjacentStageA0`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGStageMass_split_succ`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
